<title>USA: Prodigy won't access Internet child pornography.</title>
<headline>Prodigy won't access Internet child pornography.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prodigy Inc's Prodigy Services Corp said Monday it will not provide access on its servers to certain Internet newsgroups that it has concluded likely contain child pornography.</p>
<p>Access to about 20,000 other newsgroups through Prodigy servers will not be affected by this decision.</p>
<p>The move is effective immediately.</p>
</text>
